{"book":21,"chapter":7,"context":{"chapter":7,"title":"Wisdom for a Crooked World","summary":"A string of 'better' sayings commends sober reflection (mourning over feasting, rebuke over flattery, patience over pride). The Preacher then admits wisdom is beyond him, and that God made people upright but they have sought out many schemes.","background":"'The house of mourning' (v. 2) was a home in the days of grief after a death, when neighbors came to sit with the family; facing death makes the living wiser. Verses 16–18 are much debated, and many read 'be not righteous over much' as a warning against self-righteous show, not against true goodness.","customs":[{"term":"Crackling of thorns under a pot","verses":"7:6","note":"Dry thorns flare up noisily but burn out with little heat. In Hebrew it is also a pun: 'thorns' (sirim) and 'pot' (sir) sound alike."}],"watchFor":["Count the 'better' sayings in vv. 1–11.","'There is not a just man upon earth… that sinneth not' (v. 20).","Verse 29 sums up the human problem in one line."],"connections":["Proverbs 22:1","1 Kings 8:46","Romans 3:23","Genesis 1:31"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["טוֹב","tov","H2896","HAamsa","[is] good"],["שֵׁם","shem","H8034","HNcmsa","a name"],["מִשֶּׁמֶן","mishemen","H8081","HR/Ncmsa","more than ointment"],["טוֹב","tov","H2896","HAamsa","good"],["וְיוֹם","veyom","H3117","HC/Ncmsc","and [the] day of"],["הַמָּוֶת","hamavet","H4194","HTd/Ncmsa","<the> death"],["מִיּוֹם","miyom","H3117","HR/Ncmsc","more than [the] day of"],["הִוָּלְדוֹ","hivaldo","H3205","HVNcc/Sp3ms","being born he"]],"x":[[66014013,66014013,17],[20022001,20022001,16],[21004002,21004002,9],[47005008,47005008,8],[47005001,47005001,6],[50001021,50001023,6],[20027009,20027009,4],[22001003,22001003,4],[21010001,21010001,3]],"xn":9},"2":{"w":[["טוֹב","tov","H2896","HAamsa","[is] good"],["לָלֶכֶת","lalekhet","H1980","HR/Vqcc","to go"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["בֵּית","beit-","H1004","HNcmsc","a house of"],["אֵבֶל","'evel","H60","HNcmsa","mou